message: "If you use this software, please cite the software release using the metadata below."
title: "BrainFMOps-Analyze: A Quality-Aware and Reproducible Pipeline for Subject-Level Brain MRI Classification"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Sira"
    given-names: "Sirasakamol"
    affiliation: "Kunming University of Science and Technology, Kunming, China"
repository-code: "https://github.com/COMAI555/BrainFMOps-Analyze"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-08-17"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - Brain MRI
  - MLOps
  - reproducibility
  - subject-level classification
  - OASIS
abstract: >-
  BrainFMOps-Analyze is a research prototype for quality-aware and reproducible
  subject-level brain MRI classification. It provides dataset-readiness checks,
  leakage-aware subject splitting, model training and inference utilities,
  subject-level aggregation, explainability, statistical evaluation, and
  publication-support workflows. The software is intended for research and
  methodological audit only and is not a medical device or clinical
  decision-support system.
